Nicknamed the "Unibeam" prototype by fans for its distinct rectangular chest reactor housing, the Mark XIII completely abandoned red and gold in favor of a sleek, dark gunmetal grey and silver-titanium paint scheme. Tony stripped away heavy exterior armor plating to significantly reduce takeoff drag, allowing the suit to reach supersonic speeds far faster than previous iterations. Built primarily to test high-altitude maneuverability and rapid climb rates, it responded to the House Party Protocol call in Iron Man 3 before meeting its end in the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
